,"status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Corporate Resources & Governance Scrutiny & Improvement Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Growth Scrutiny & Improvement Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-18","committee":"Climate & Environment Scrutiny & Improvement Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Governance Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Council tax premiums on second homes and long-term empty properties are to continue","lead":"Council tax premiums represent discretionary revenue-raising that indicates how the council is responding to funding pressures and managing its tax base.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"Cabinet Report to Borough Council Financial Outturn Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11799/11799.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a33.5m additional borrowing approved for new Enterprise Resource Planning system","lead":"A \u00a33.5m borrowing decision materially affects the council's debt and prudential borrowing headroom; lenders need to understand the business case and whether this competes with service delivery priorities.","iso":"2026-07-30","paper_title":"Cabinet Report to Borough Council Financial Outturn Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11799/11799.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Early years funding recovery is failing when providers make no claim in the following term","lead":"This is a control failure on grant distribution; overpayments represent money the council has distributed incorrectly that it is unable to recover due to process gaps.","iso":"2026-07-20","paper_title":"5.6 Annex 1 - Internal audit progress report (July 2026)","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11763/11763.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Borough Council","paper_title":"Cabinet Report to Borough Council Financial Outturn Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11799/11799.pdf","headline":"Council tax premiums on second homes and long-term empty properties are to continue","detail":"Cabinet confirms continued application of council tax premiums following assessment against statutory guidance. The assessment concluded these are appropriate, proportionate, and consistent with the statutory framework and council's strategic and financial objectives.","category":"income","matters":"Council tax premiums represent discretionary revenue-raising that indicates how the council is responding to funding pressures and managing its tax base.","figures":"No amounts specified","quote":"Recommends that Full Council confirms and approves the continued application of council tax premiums on second homes and long-term empty properties","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-30","committee":"Borough Council","paper_title":"Cabinet Report to Borough Council Financial Outturn Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11799/11799.pdf","headline":"\u00a33.5m additional borrowing approved for new Enterprise Resource Planning system","detail":"Cabinet recommends Full Council approval of \u00a33.5 million additional borrowing to fund procurement and implementation of a new ERP system. This is a material capital investment decision with borrowing implications for the council's debt profile.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A \u00a33.5m borrowing decision materially affects the council's debt and prudential borrowing headroom; lenders need to understand the business case and whether this competes with service delivery priorities.","figures":"\u00a33.5 million","quote":"recommending to Full Council the approval of an additional \u00a33.5 million borrowing for the procurement and implementation of a new Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"5.6 Annex 1 - Internal audit progress report (July 2026)","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11763/11763.pdf","headline":"Early years funding recovery is failing when providers make no claim in the following term","detail":"The audit found a systematic control weakness: when the council attempts to recover overpayments to early years providers, recovery consistently fails where the provider makes no claim in the subsequent term. This leaves overpayments unrecovered on a dedicated funding stream the council administers.","category":"income","matters":"This is a control failure on grant distribution; overpayments represent money the council has distributed incorrectly that it is unable to recover due to process gaps.","figures":"No amounts quantified, but the issue affects ongoing overpayment recovery","quote":"Where recovery action is taken, this consistently fails to correct overpayments where no funding is claimed in the following term.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"9.1 2026 Annual Governance Statement - working draft for Gov Cttee - App 1","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11782/11782.pdf","headline":"2026/27 budget allocates only \u00a36m to rebuild reserves described as urgently needed","detail":"Recognizing critically low reserves, the 2026/27 budget has allocated \u00a36m to replenish the MTFS reserve. The statement explicitly describes this as an 'urgent need' to rebuild reserves 'both immediately and incrementally over the MTFS period' to restore 'safer and more sustainable level of financial protection'.","category":"reserves","matters":"\u00a36m allocation against 'critically low' reserves over a multi-year period confirms severe reserve depletion and indicates incremental recovery will take years, leaving the council at heightened risk in the interim","figures":"\u00a36m allocated to MTFS Reserve in 2026/27 budget; described as starting a process over MTFS period","quote":"There is an urgent need to rebuild reserves, both immediately and incrementally over the MTFS period, to restore a safer and more sustainable level of financial protection. The Budget for 2026/27 starts the process of addressing this by allocating \u00a36 million to replenish the MTFS Reserve.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance Committee","paper_title":"9.1 2026 Annual Governance Statement - working draft for Gov Cttee - App 1","paper_url":"https://rcbc.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s11782/11782.pdf","headline":"New escalation procedure for audit actions indicates previous non-delivery of recommendations","detail":"A new escalation procedure has been introduced during 2026/27 to ensure robust monitoring of audit action delivery. Where audit actions fall overdue, they will be escalated and action holders can be requested to appear before Governance Committee. This implies previous audit actions were not being completed on time.","category":"audit","matters":"Audit actions are improvements to control environment weaknesses; failure to implement them on schedule indicates management capacity issues or governance culture challenges in addressing control gaps","figures":"Quarterly reporting of outstanding audit actions introduced; escalation to Governance Committee for significantly overdue items","quote":"A new escalation procedure has been introduced during 2026/27 to ensure robust monitoring of the delivery of audit actions and recommendations. A quarterly report on outstanding audit actions is presented by the Assistant Director of Finance to the Executive Management Team, alongside the existing reporting to Risk Management Group. If audit actions fall overdue, this will provide the initial step for escalation.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-30"},"name":"Redcar & Cleveland UA","findings_total":94,"news_drafts_total":3}}